  "details": "<p>The\u00a0<em>Pons Aelius\u00a0</em>is one of 9 Tiber River bridges included on map 43 of the\u00a0<em>Barrington Atlas.</em>These bridges are not necessarily specified by name, given the scale of the map, but the compilers have used Richardson's 1992 listing as their guide.</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "The Pons Aelius or Aelian Bridge (now Ponte Sant'Angelo) was completed by Hadrian in AD 134 to span the Tiber opposite the new mausoleum of the emperor.",
